From 38280861cb89dd791c8360e5797c38d3259b347d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hans van Essen <hans@expaso.nl>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 22:24:23 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] nvidia: skip teardown in nv_pci_shutdown() while GPU is
 hibernate-suspended

With the documented hibernation setup (NVreg_PreserveVideoMemoryAllocations=1
plus nvidia-hibernate.service), the system hangs after the hibernation image
has been written and never powers off. The last console line is
"[nvidia-drm] Unloading driver".

Sequence:
  1. nvidia-sleep.sh writes "hibernate" to /proc/driver/nvidia/suspend:
     nv_set_system_power_state() takes nv_system_pm_lock for write and
     suspends the GPU (NV_FLAG_SUSPENDED).
  2. The kernel freezes devices (nv_pmops_freeze), creates the snapshot and
     thaws devices to write the image. nv_pmops_thaw() is a no-op, so the GPU
     stays suspended and nv_system_pm_lock stays write-locked.
  3. After the image is written, HibernateMode=shutdown (or reboot, or a
     failed ACPI S4 entry) calls kernel_power_off() -> device_shutdown() ->
     nv_pci_shutdown() -> nv_pci_remove_helper() -> nvidia_modeset_remove()
     -> nv-drm unload, i.e. a full driver teardown against a suspended GPU.
     This never completes.

The machine is about to lose power and the GPU state was already saved by
the suspend path, so a teardown is neither needed nor possible here. When
the device is still NV_FLAG_SUSPENDED, only clear bus mastering and return.
Normal shutdown and reboot are unaffected because the flag is not set then.

Tested on an RTX 5080 Laptop GPU (GB203, ASUS GU605CW) with 615.71.09 and
Linux 7.3-rc5: before, hibernation hung at "Unloading driver" every time
(also with 610.57.04); after, the system powers off right after the image is
written and resumes normally.

Signed-off-by: Hans van Essen <hans@expaso.nl>
---
 kernel-open/nvidia/nv-pci.c | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/kernel-open/nvidia/nv-pci.c b/kernel-open/nvidia/nv-pci.c
index 48d8b78..176d56e 100644
--- a/kernel-open/nvidia/nv-pci.c
+++ b/kernel-open/nvidia/nv-pci.c
@@ -2978,6 +2978,18 @@ nv_pci_shutdown(struct pci_dev *pci_dev)
         return;
     }
 
+    /*
+     * Hibernation power-off: thaw is a no-op, so the GPU is still suspended
+     * (procfs hibernate holds nv_system_pm_lock) and a full teardown hangs.
+     */
+    if (nvl->nv_state.flags & NV_FLAG_SUSPENDED)
+    {
+#ifdef CONFIG_PCI
+        pci_clear_master(pci_dev);
+#endif
+        return;
+    }
+
 #if defined(CONFIG_PM_DEVFREQ)
     nv_pci_tegra_unregister_devfreq(pci_dev);
 #endif
-- 
